# Who is asked to review.
#
# Both people who can approve a change own every file. GitHub never requests a
# review from a pull request's own author, so a change by either of them asks
# the other, and a pull request opened by Dependabot asks both.
#
# This is a request, not a gate. The ruleset on main already requires an
# approving review from somebody other than the last pusher and does not require
# a code owner's review, so this file changes who is notified and nothing about
# what may merge. It exists because Dependabot's pull requests request no
# reviewer at all, and two of them sat unseen in nobody's queue.
